meta {
  name: CreateThread — launch a subagent
  type: grpc
  seq: 2
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.DemandService/CreateThread
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "demand_id": "dem-1",
      "key": "forense-db",
      "card": {
        "purpose": "A forensic reading of the database: a divergence in instalment 12",
        "tools": ["mcp:mysql"],
        "model": "claude-haiku-4-5",
        "effort": "medium",
        "budget_micros": 500000
      },
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0013, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  It launches a subagent with its own card: purpose, tools, model and a slice of
  the budget (ADR-0007).

  The model comes from the menu of the account's agent integrations; the one who
  chooses is the `ModelRouter` (ADR-0008). Its own thread — no mixed timelines.
}
